    <body>
      <div type="work" n="271">
        <pb n="307"/>
        <head>Another on the Monks When He Had Returned from the Visitation of the Monasteries<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <head>271 — i — VII. — <quote>My tears became to me bread day and night</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/>.</head>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="1">When I take to mind the men who practise the Nazirite<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/> life and [bear in their bodies<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/> the life-giving mortality of <persName>Jesus</persName><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/>, God the Word who became incarnate, and constantly by day<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/> and night meditate upon and devote themselves to the law of the Lord, and with their throats shoot forth the glories and sweet praises<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> of God like fountains, I wail over my miserable life, [which I see<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a8" target="#n8" n="8"/> to have grown old and been consumed<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a9" target="#n9" n="9"/> in vain profitless labours; and with affliction and sorrow<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a10" target="#n10" n="10"/> of heart I cry, <quote>Who will give water for my head, and a plentiful well of tears for my eyes?<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a11" target="#n11" n="11"/> in order that, having<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a12" target="#n12" n="12"/> consciousness or <pb n="308"/> knowledge of my evil deeds, I may incline<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a13" target="#n13" n="13"/> <persName>Christ</persName> the great in mercy toward me and be admitted to his great clemencies</quote>.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 1</orig></choice> June 514 (Hom. 61).</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 2</orig></choice> Ps. xlii, 4.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 3</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>monastic</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>carry about in the body</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 5</orig></choice> II Cor. iv, 7-10 <quote>But we have..... from us. In everything..... perish not. At all times..... in our bodies</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 6</orig></choice> Ps. i, 2 (not quoted).</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 7</orig></choice> Id. cxlix, 6 (not quoted).</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 8</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>seeing it</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n9" target="#a9" n="9"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 9</orig></choice> Id. xxxi, 10 (not quoted).</note>
        <note xml:id="n10" target="#a10" n="10"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 10</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>miseries</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n11" target="#a11" n="11"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 11</orig></choice> Jer. ix, 1 LXX <quote>Who will give water for my head and wells of tears for my eyes? and I will weep over this people day and night, over the slain one of the daughter of my people</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n12" target="#a12" n="12"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 307, n. 12</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>by</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n13" target="#a13" n="13"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 308, n. 1</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>inclining</quote>.</note>
      </noteGrp>
